  "summary": "Added a confirmation-gated audit stop command, Reports Stop Audit control, stale-active progress handling after reopen, and matching route/DOM inventories.",
  "reason": "Closing and reopening during a large audit could leave stale active audit progress with Start Audit clickable and no operator stop path.",
  "affected_areas": [
    "code",
    "contracts",
    "docs",
    "generated",
    "process-control",
    "tests",
    "webview"
  ],
  "behavior_before": "Reports could show an active or stale audit with Start Audit available, no elapsed/stop affordance after reopen, and no backend route to stop audit-scoped child processes.",
  "behavior_after": "Reports disables Start while active or stale-active audit progress is visible, enables Stop Audit, and posts /api/audit/stop with confirm_stop=true so the backend terminates audit-scoped spawned and related processes and writes stopped audit progress.",
